{"name":"Fire Island","hex":"#d95137","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fire Island","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The large center island of the outer barrier islands parallel to the south shore of Long Island, New York, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fire_Island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fire Island","blocks":[{"text":"Fire Island is the large center island of the outer barrier islands parallel to the South Shore of Long Island in the U.S. state of New York."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Fire_Island-NY-USA-Location_Map-01.svg/330px-Fire_Island-NY-USA-Location_Map-01.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_Island"},{"title":"Fire Island (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Fire Island is a 2022 American romantic comedy film directed by Andrew Ahn and written by and starring Joel Kim Booster. The film co-stars Bowen Yang, Conrad Ricamora, James Scully, and Margaret Cho. The plot follows a group of gay friends on vacation at the eponymous New York island, where romance becomes complicated by classism in a story inspired by Jane Austen's Pride and Prejudice. Distributed and produced by Searchlight Pictures, the film was released June 3, 2022 on Hulu, to generally positive reviews."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/Fire_Island_Movie_Poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_Island_(film)"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/FireIslandLighthouse_080507.jpg/500px-FireIslandLighthouse_080507.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/FireIslandLighthouse_080507.jpg/500px-FireIslandLighthouse_080507.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fire Island Lighthouse, east of Robert Moses field 5","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFireIslandLighthouse_080507.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/FI_Lighthouse_pan.jpg/500p